('Feature_01_Stock_Intraday', 'close', 'ticker x timeframe (5m, 15m, 1h, 4h) x bar_time', 'Price', 'Per bar of the row''s timeframe (one period = one bar). Closing price for the ticker in the bar.', 'Direct copy of price_stock_idx_intraday.close.', 'price_stock_idx_intraday', 'price_stock_idx_intraday: ticker, timeframe, bar_time, session_date, open, high, low, close, volume (stocks only; IDX_Stock_Universe "Security Type" index excluded)', 'Current bar', '1 bar', 'source price unit', 'Never NULL for a stored row; source close must exist and be nonnegative.', 'idx-intraday-cron feature step (intraday_feature_queue) after each daily load; once by the backfill job', 'The 120 bars before the first changed bar are read as context, so each written bar equals a full-history calculation; rows are written from that bar to the end of the series.', 'v1', true, 'MEASURE', ARRAY['AVG', 'MEDIAN', 'MIN', 'MAX', 'COUNT']::text[], 'CONTEXTUAL', true, false, 'Close-of-bar value, loaded once a day after the session close plus Equity_Market_Schedule.finality_delay_minutes; not available intraday in real time and not exposed to the AI yet.', false, 'Historical cross-sectional use requires SURVIVORSHIP_BIAS_WARNING because Feature 1 was constructed through the current stock universe. Intraday bars are split-adjusted as TradingView gives them at load time; a series whose whole stored scale changed is not written until rescaled (loader verdict SCALE_CHANGED). Session completeness: join price_stock_idx_intraday_quality on (timeframe, session_date).', 'Interpret close by its sign, magnitude, null state, own history, peer distribution and market regime; no universal high-is-good rule applies. Definition: Closing price for the ticker in the bar.', 'Use close as the observed nominal closing-price level for the ticker/date, as an input to validated return or drawdown comparisons, and for exact source-to-Feature reconciliation. Compare cross-ticker nominal prices only when that scale difference is analytically intended.', 'Window counts are observed transaction/bars, not calendar days. Respect the NULL contract: Never NULL for a stored row; source close must exist and be nonnegative. Do not treat a single high, low, positive, negative or extreme bar as predictive evidence without historical validation and appropriate benchmarks.', 'CALCULATION_VERIFIED', ARRAY['database/migrations/20261031_004_intraday_features.sql', 'verification/intraday_features/README.md', 'apps/idx-price-cron/intraday_features.py', 'apps/idx-price-cron/test_intraday_features.py', 'database/migrations/20260912_001_create_feature_01_stock_daily.sql', 'database/migrations/20260913_001_create_feature_catalog.sql', 'DATABASE_CHANGELOG.md#2026-09-12-create-and-backfill-feature-01-stock-daily']::text[]),
('Feature_01_Stock_Intraday', 'volume', 'ticker x timeframe (5m, 15m, 1h, 4h) x bar_time', 'Volume', 'Per bar of the row''s timeframe (one period = one bar). Trading volume reported for the ticker in the bar.', 'Direct copy of price_stock_idx_intraday.volume.', 'price_stock_idx_intraday', 'price_stock_idx_intraday: ticker, timeframe, bar_time, session_date, open, high, low, close, volume (stocks only; IDX_Stock_Universe "Security Type" index excluded)', 'Current bar', '1 bar', 'Shares', 'NULL for a universe-classified index without source volume. Stock volume is required and nonnegative; missing volume is never imputed as zero.', 'idx-intraday-cron feature step (intraday_feature_queue) after each daily load; once by the backfill job', 'The 120 bars before the first changed bar are read as context, so each written bar equals a full-history calculation; rows are written from that bar to the end of the series.', 'v1', true, 'MEASURE', ARRAY['AVG', 'MEDIAN', 'MIN', 'MAX', 'COUNT']::text[], 'CONTEXTUAL', true, false, 'Close-of-bar value, loaded once a day after the session close plus Equity_Market_Schedule.finality_delay_minutes; not available intraday in real time and not exposed to the AI yet.', false, 'Historical cross-sectional use requires SURVIVORSHIP_BIAS_WARNING because Feature 1 was constructed through the current stock universe. Intraday bars are split-adjusted as TradingView gives them at load time; a series whose whole stored scale changed is not written until rescaled (loader verdict SCALE_CHANGED). Session completeness: join price_stock_idx_intraday_quality on (timeframe, session_date).', 'Interpret volume by its sign, magnitude, null state, own history, peer distribution and market regime; no universal high-is-good rule applies. Definition: Trading volume reported for the ticker in the bar.', 'Use volume to assess participation or abnormal activity relative to the documented volume window and available history.', 'Missing index volume is NULL, never a synthetic zero. Ordinary stock volume must exist. Volume-dependent metrics remain NULL when their required bars are unavailable.', 'CALCULATION_VERIFIED', ARRAY['database/migrations/20261031_004_intraday_features.sql', 'verification/intraday_features/README.md', 'apps/idx-price-cron/intraday_features.py', 'apps/idx-price-cron/test_intraday_features.py', 'database/migrations/20260912_001_create_feature_01_stock_daily.sql', 'database/migrations/20260913_001_create_feature_catalog.sql', 'DATABASE_CHANGELOG.md#2026-09-12-create-and-backfill-feature-01-stock-daily']::text[]),
('Feature_01_Stock_Intraday', 'close_1bar_ago', 'ticker x timeframe (5m, 15m, 1h, 4h) x bar_time', 'Price', 'Per bar of the row''s timeframe (one period = one bar). Closing price one prior bar earlier for the same ticker.', 'LAG(close, 1) OVER (PARTITION BY ticker ORDER BY bar_time).', 'price_stock_idx_intraday', 'price_stock_idx_intraday: ticker, timeframe, bar_time, session_date, open, high, low, close, volume (stocks only; IDX_Stock_Universe "Security Type" index excluded)', '1 prior bar', '2 bars including current bar', 'source price unit', 'NULL when fewer than 2 bars exist for the ticker.', 'idx-intraday-cron feature step (intraday_feature_queue) after each daily load; once by the backfill job', 'The 120 bars before the first changed bar are read as context, so each written bar equals a full-history calculation; rows are written from that bar to the end of the series.', 'v1', true, 'MEASURE', ARRAY['AVG', 'MEDIAN', 'MIN', 'MAX', 'COUNT']::text[], 'CONTEXTUAL', true, false, 'Close-of-bar value, loaded once a day after the session close plus Equity_Market_Schedule.finality_delay_minutes; not available intraday in real time and not exposed to the AI yet.', false, 'Historical cross-sectional use requires SURVIVORSHIP_BIAS_WARNING because Feature 1 was constructed through the current stock universe. Intraday bars are split-adjusted as TradingView gives them at load time; a series whose whole stored scale changed is not written until rescaled (loader verdict SCALE_CHANGED). Session completeness: join price_stock_idx_intraday_quality on (timeframe, session_date).', 'Interpret close_1bar_ago by its sign, magnitude, null state, own history, peer distribution and market regime; no universal high-is-good rule applies. Definition: Closing price one prior bar earlier for the same ticker.', 'Use close_1bar_ago as the documented prior trading-bar price reference to verify or explain the corresponding trailing return, volatility or drawdown calculation; do not rank different 